Parts of the system DNS configuration, hosts-file handling, server selection
and timeout calculations follow c-ares 1.34.9. Its DNS message and record parsers
also serve as behavioral references.
https://github.com/c-ares/c-ares/tree/v1.34.9/src/lib

ares_hosts_file.c, ares_init.c, ares_metrics.c, ares_process.c,
ares_sysconfig_win.c, ares_update_servers.c, ares_dns_parse.c, ares_dns_name.c,
ares_dns_write.c, ares_dns_record.c, ares_dns_mapping.c, ares_dns_multistring.c,
ares_buf.c, ares_query.c, ares_gethostbyaddr.c, ares_addrinfo2hostent.c,
ares_parse_into_addrinfo.c and the legacy ares_parse_*_reply.c parsers

